            <div xml:id="d549">

                <pb facs="0752" n="740" sameAs="frus:frus1946v08/pg740"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Korea)/9–1446: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Political Adviser in Korea</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Langdon</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-09-24T18:00:00-04:00">September 24, 1946—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>129. Report apparent complete rift in leftist front (urtel 108 Sept 14 latest received here) presumed to be background
                    upon which press reports (UP and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">NY Times</hi>) appearing here are based. These stories
                    indicate progress in unification movement favorable prelude to plan <pb
                        facs="0753" n="741" xml:id="pg741"/> for holding election selecting
                    delegates to proposed legislative assembly.</p>
                <p>Stories also indicate details of election plan to be made public soon but
                    ambiguous as to whether elections are to be held within 2 months or assembly to
                    be convened within that period. Your comments would be appreciated together with
                    suggestions you or CG
                    USAFIK may have as to manner in which Dept through releases here might usefully
                    contribute in focusing attention on current developments.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clayton</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
